The attached image (Figure 5) demonstrates Nano-11's ability to facilitate antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Panel A shows flow cytometry plots where ovalbumin (OVA) complexed with Nano-11 (OVA+N11) results in higher OVA mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) in myeloid cells compared to soluble OVA or OVA with aluminum hydroxide (OVA+AH). Panel B quantifies this, illustrating significantly higher OVA MFI in cells treated with OVA+N11 on both Day 1 and Day 2. Panel C indicates that Nano-11 significantly increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells in the lymph nodes by Day 2, supporting its role in enhanced antigen delivery to these key antigen-presenting cells.